WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.159 --> 00:00:01.200
CHELSEA FISCHBACH: Hello.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.630
Today, I'm going
to be showing you

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:04.610
a new add-on for
Google Cloud that

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:08.600
will allow you to seamlessly
import, update, manage,

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.780
and share data from Salesforce
using Google Sheets.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.250
My name is Chelsea Fischbach.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.740
I'm from the global
technology partnerships team.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.810
And we're going to
be talking about how

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.940
you can use this
add-on to improve

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.450
the collaboration of your
team and save time every day

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.130
with your Salesforce workflows.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.850
Let's dive in.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:31.450
Let's start by looking at a
lead report in Salesforce.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.120
You can see here
that it's broken down

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.190
by status and by lead owner.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.560
Today, we're going to be
focusing on a use case

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.140
where you're at the
end of a quarter

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.840
and you're looking to update
your lead data to better

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.110
protect your sales for
the following quarter.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.940
This is just an
example though, and you

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.480
can use any object that you have
configured in your Salesforce

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.080
instance.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.190
Let's go ahead and
jump over to the add-on

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.350
to see what this data will
look like in Google Sheets.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.080
So you can see here that we
have a sheet already open.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.250
Let's go ahead and
open up the add-on.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.210
If you don't have the
add-on already installed,

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.770
you can get it from
the get add-ons menu.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.170
So let's open up the add-on.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.940
Here, you can see
all the options

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.880
that are available for you
to take using the add-on.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.320
Let's start by
pulling in the data

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.720
from that report we
were just looking at.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.330
From the reports option, you
can choose a recently run

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.520
report or search
any report that's

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.030
in your Salesforce instance.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.900
Let's go ahead and pull up
the leads report by status

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.050
as we are looking at
in the previous view.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.660
We're going to import this data
to the current sheet, which

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.496
will wipe out the data
that we have there.

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:39.620
If you want to keep the
data in your current sheet,

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.430
just open up a new tab.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.300
You can see here all the
data from that report loaded

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.510
in the sheet.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.752
We can see the
status, the owner.

00:01:47.752 --> 00:01:49.460
We can also see a lot
of demographic data

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.660
about the lead.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.640
This data can be
really helpful when

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.190
you're looking to share data
with people who might not

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:58.070
have access to Salesforce, or
when you're doing those year

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.130
end reports and you want to
use all the power of Sheets

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:05.190
to build charts and to just
make better business decisions.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:09.229
Now let's look at what we can
do if we import a custom query.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.720
From the import option,
you can choose any object

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.010
that you have access to in
your Salesforce database.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:16.760
Let's go ahead and
pull up the lead object

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:19.140
that we were looking
at previously.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.670
You can also, at this point,
load the last data import

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:25.640
settings to quickly start
the process if you previously

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.150
were running imports
using the add-on.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.500
With the lead object
selected, let's go ahead

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.982
and look at the fields that we
can import from the next step.

00:02:33.982 --> 00:02:35.690
Here, you can choose
from the fields that

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:37.250
are available for this object.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.250
Today, we're going to be
importing the state as well

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.360
as the status.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.520
And this allows us to focus
on the data set that we're

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:50.450
most interested in achieving.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:55.730
Let's also import the
company name and the lead ID.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.890
The lead ID is very
important because it

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:02.510
allows us to know what
object we want to update.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.430
Finally, let's filter
the data that we're

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.260
going to be updating.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.360
First, we're going
to choose the state.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.490
And we're going to
filter on California

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.020
because that's the
territory that we

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.372
want to make changes to today.

00:03:15.372 --> 00:03:16.955
We're also going to
choose the status.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.970
And you can see here that
we load in the pick list

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.730
from Salesforce, so we follow
all of the data formatting

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:27.700
requirements that you already
have configured in Salesforce.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.770
Let's select contacted
to focus on leads

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:34.392
that we've reached out to,
but haven't gotten back to us.

00:03:34.392 --> 00:03:35.850
One thing I do want
to point out is

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.310
that we do have a
SOQL editor available.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.250
This will allow you
to customize the query

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:45.690
further than is available
in our graphic interface.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.467
Now that we've chosen the data
that we want to import, let's

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:49.550
go ahead and get the data.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.620
You can see here that we pulled
in the state, the status,

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.350
the company, and the ID.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:01.670
These are exactly the
fields that we asked for.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:06.130
And so we're ready to
start making our updates.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:07.860
Let's go into status,
and we're going

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:11.010
to choose to unqualify
some of these leads.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.560
So we can edit this just
like any other sheet

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:14.840
in our instance.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:17.850
And we can use formulas
or functions, whatever is

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.589
needed to make those updates.

00:04:19.589 --> 00:04:21.720
You can see here that we've
updated several of them

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:22.860
to unqualified.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.720
We're going to go
into the update flow

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.720
to see how we can make the
change on the Salesforce side.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.510
Inside the updates
flow, we'll see

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.920
that the options
that we have selected

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.990
are highlighted in yellow.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:37.660
This allows us to
know which objects

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:41.280
we're going to be updating
when we make these changes.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.860
It's very easy to make changes.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.650
We just choose a new selection
and hit refresh the selected

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:46.700
range.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.680
You can see here
that the new options

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.730
are highlighted in yellow now.

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:53.090
Now that we have the
correct selection,

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:57.350
we can go ahead and confirm the
data that we want to update.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.630
You'll see that we make
some smart decisions to try

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:02.000
to make it easy for you to
make updates to your data

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.480
through this process.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.630
If we look at the lead
object that we're updating,

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.700
we'll see that it's
already selected, which

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.270
we can tell from the ID number.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.790
You can see that there are
three functions available for us

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.030
to make changes.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.640
The first is
insert, which allows

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.494
you to insert a new record.

00:05:17.494 --> 00:05:18.910
The second is
update, which allows

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.160
you to update existing records.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.230
And the third is
insert or update,

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:26.440
which will update a data
point if it already exists

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.970
or insert a new one.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.040
Let's go ahead and choose
update because that's

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.552
what we want to be doing today.

00:05:32.552 --> 00:05:34.010
You can see here
that we've already

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:37.310
identified the ID in column
D, and that the results

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.710
of our update will
spit out in column E.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.645
And this is just the first
column with no data in it.

00:05:42.645 --> 00:05:44.520
So if you want to change
it, you can do that.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.030
Just make sure that there is
no data going to be overwritten

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.680
when you make that change.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.140
Now we can complete
the last step

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:53.840
before we make the change, which
is confirming the data that we

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:54.800
want to update.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.770
Today, we're going to unselect
the state and the company data

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.510
because we didn't
make any changes.

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:01.970
And it'll just make the
import a little faster

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:04.940
because we do run validation
on every single object

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.170
that we update.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:09.530
So let's go ahead and execute
and see what happens here.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:12.620
You can see that the data
has been updated successfully

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:15.140
as indicated by the
green message in column

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:18.020
E. If there is an error,
it will be marked in red.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.520
And we'll show you
the error message

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.710
that we get back from
Salesforce, which

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:25.580
makes it very easy for you to
be able to troubleshoot the data

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.640
as you're making changes.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:29.780
So there you have it.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.450
Now you can see how
you can seamlessly

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:34.810
import, update, manage,
and share Salesforce data

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:36.430
using Google Sheets.

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:38.950
If you want to check out this
add-on for your organization,

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.570
check out the link
below to install it

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:43.159
from the G Suite marketplace.

00:06:43.159 --> 00:06:45.200
If you like this video,
please like and subscribe

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.730
